    "https://newmanuniversity.applytojob.com/apply/jobs/details/VfdVNvxT4D": {
      "title": "Student - Admissions Ambassador",
      "description": "JazzHR » Job Listings « Back to Jobs Newman University Student - Admissions Ambassador Admissions - Wichita, KS - Part Time Job Summary: The Admissions team seeks enthusiastic and dedicated students with a strong commitment to the University. Ideal candidates will have a passion for sharing their campus experience and expertise with prospective students, families and other guests visiting Newman University. Ambassador Work Performed: Guiding campus tours for prospective Newman University students and families, in person. Guiding campus tours for various other guests, including new staff & faculty. Assist Admissions Counselors in school visits from High Schools, Middle Schools and Elementary Schools. Participate in event days and student panels, sharing your Newman experience. (Typically 2-3 Saturday events in the Fall and Spring.) Work 5 to 20 hours each week. Complete University-required trainings. Requirements: Be a full-time Newman University student, enrolled in 12 or more credit hours per semester (First Year students are welcome to apply as well as upper classman students) Must be legally authorized to work in the United States A high degree of commitment and reliability Excellent communication skills Flexibility and adaptability for various visit experiences and guests Passionate about Newman University Respect for confidentiality and professionalism at all times, especially when guests are present Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, times vary. Potential for weekend and evening shifts as recruitment events are scheduled. Pay: $8.25 per hour Founded in 1933, Newman University is a liberal arts institution grounded in Catholic values and traditions, yet is respectful of all faiths. At Newman you'll find people, programs, organizations and activities designed to educate the mind and inspire the spirit. Our low instructor-to-student ratio and collaborative faculty contribute to a positive learning environment. We are a sponsored ministry of the