      "title": "Student - Navigator Peer Guides",
      "description": "JazzHR » Job Listings « Back to Jobs Newman University Student - Navigator Peer Guides Navigator - Wichita, KS - Part Time The Navigator Program is seeking enthusiastic and dependable Peer Guides to support incoming students in Flight Planning classes for Fall 2026 . Compensation: $400 stipend Position Responsibilities: Peer Guides play an important role in helping new students transition to university life. Responsibilities include: Serving as a resource for incoming freshmen on social, personal, and academic issues. Leading discussions and activities during Flight Planning classes. Helping new students and their families become familiar with university policies, procedures, campus resources, and student activities. Supporting the overall success of the Navigator Program. Performing additional duties as assigned. Qualified applicants should: Have a minimum cumulative GPA of 3.0 . Demonstrate leadership and strong communication skills. Be responsible, reliable, creative, energetic, and self-motivated. Work well as part of a team and maintain a positive attitude and sense of humor. Understand and support the goals and philosophy of the Navigator Program. Must be legally authorized to work in the United States. Why Apply? This is a great opportunity to develop leadership skills, mentor new students, make a positive impact on campus, and gain valuable experience working with incoming freshmen. Apply today and help new students successfully navigate their first year! Founded in 1933, Newman University is a liberal arts institution grounded in Catholic values and traditions, yet is respectful of all faiths. At Newman you'll find people, programs, organizations and activities designed to educate the mind and inspire the spirit. Our low instructor-to-student ratio and collaborative faculty contribute to a positive learning environment. We are a sponsored ministry of the Adorers of the Blood of Christ, US Region. We invite you to join us in our work of