    "https://newmanuniversity.applytojob.com/apply/jobs/details/djbKoBeO7h": {
      "title": "Student - Science Courses Lab Assistant",
      "description": "JazzHR » Job Listings « Back to Jobs Newman University Student - Science Courses Lab Assistant Division of Math and Science - Wichita, KS - Part Time General Description: The Science & Math department is looking for students to assist in the lab portion of Fall 2026 classes. Must have previously completed a lab course in the subject matter you will be assisting. Duties and Responsibilities: Attend your assigned section and actively participate in the student learning process. Assist in the evaluation and assessment of lab reports as directed by the course instructor. Maintain confidentiality of all coursework and assignments, grades, and any material on any graded assignments throughout the course Aid the instructor during class, including supervising the lab, ensuring students perform activities correctly and helping to answer questions when possible Monitor and notify the instructor if supplies for future labs are low and need to be reordered Assist with lab prep and clean up Additional duties include cleaning and disinfecting the lab before and/or after labs Position Requirements: Continued full-time student status (minimum of 12 credit hours). Successful completion of corresponding lab course with a grade of B or higher, preferably at Newman University. Must be legally authorized to work in the United States. Number of hours per week: 5 Rate of Pay: $8.25 per hour Founded in 1933, Newman University is a liberal arts institution grounded in Catholic values and traditions, yet is respectful of all faiths. At Newman you'll find people, programs, organizations and activities designed to educate the mind and inspire the spirit. Our low instructor-to-student ratio and collaborative faculty contribute to a positive learning environment. We are a sponsored ministry of the Adorers of the Blood of Christ, US Region. We invite you to join us in our work of empowering our graduates to transform society! Newman University participates in E-Verify and wi