      "title": "Student - Sports Information Assistant",
      "description": "JazzHR » Job Listings « Back to Jobs Newman University Student - Sports Information Assistant Athletics - Wichita, KS - Part Time General Description: The Newman University Athletic Department is looking for reliable and responsible student workers to assist the Assistant Athletic Director of Communications. This involves attending and working during multiple sporting events. Responsibilities: Set up and tear down before and after games. Record live statistics and update social media during games. Assist with scoreboard operation, public addresses, and music and audio functions during games. Operate the camera and live streaming monitor. Occasionally write games stories and provide graphic design or photography. Requirements: Must be legally authorized to work in the United States. Must be a current Newman University student enrolled full-time (12 credit hours per semester). General knowledge of athletic events with a background in sports preferred. Must be punctual and dependable. Some heavy lifting and moving of equipment. Ability to sit or stand for extended periods of time. Number of hours per week : Max of 20 hours Days and times : Varies week to week with most hours being evenings and weekends Rate of Pay : $8.25 per hour Founded in 1933, Newman University is a liberal arts institution grounded in Catholic values and traditions, yet is respectful of all faiths. At Newman you'll find people, programs, organizations and activities designed to educate the mind and inspire the spirit. Our low instructor-to-student ratio and collaborative faculty contribute to a positive learning environment. We are a sponsored ministry of the Adorers of the Blood of Christ, US Region. We invite you to join us in our work of empowering our graduates to transform society! Newman University participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with Form I-9 information to confirm that new employees are authorized to work in the U.S. US Immigration law